---
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout
  title="Manifesto"
  description="Why Kalaris Labs is building self-improving scientific research infrastructure for everyone."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="site-container page-hero-grid">
        <p class="eyebrow">Manifesto / v1.0</p>
        <div>
          <h1>Research is complicated. It doesn’t have to be.</h1>
          <p class="page-lede">
            Self-improving scientific research infrastructure for the
            democratization of discovery.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="editorial-section section-rule">
      <div class="site-container editorial-grid">
        <p class="eyebrow">The friction / 01</p>
        <div class="prose-large">
          <h2>Discovery is buried under setup.</h2>
          <p>
            Researchers lose valuable time configuring environments, stitching
            together tools, managing citations, navigating repositories, and
            rebuilding context that should never have been lost.
          </p>
          <p>
            That burden does more than slow experienced teams. It raises the
            entry cost for high-school students, non-computer-scientists,
            independent researchers, and anyone without access to a well-funded
            institution.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section dark-band">
      <div class="site-container editorial-grid">
        <p class="eyebrow">The direction / 02</p>
        <div class="prose-large">
          <h2>Infrastructure that learns from the research.</h2>
          <p>
            Kalaris Labs is building an agent-powered infrastructure layer for
            scientific discovery, designed so researchers can stay closer to
            questions, experiments, and execution.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our premise is recursive self-improvement: the system should adapt
            to workflows, repositories, iterations, and papers, preserving what
            was learned and carrying it forward into the next cycle.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section section-rule">
      <div class="site-container editorial-grid">
        <p class="eyebrow">The promise / 03</p>
        <div class="prose-large">
          <h2>
            Not research for a select few. Research for everyone doing the work.
          </h2>
          <p>
            The ambition is not to replace researchers. It is to give more
            people the operational leverage to do rigorous work, follow
            difficult questions, and turn curiosity into evidence.
          </p>
          <p>Because the next breakthrough can come from anywhere.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/research"
              >Read our research →</a
            ><a class="button button-ghost" href="/company/careers"
              >Build with us</a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
